<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.9.1: Finding a Solution through Substitution</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02231</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.9.1: Finding a Solution through Substitution</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d2b11d8e-4bc6-42eb-8989-0eeca45745b4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Let's try to find at least one solution to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>35</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Create a table of values. In column 1, enter the whole numbers between 0 and 10 to represent values of x. In column 2, evaluate the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>35</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> using the values for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00003">Write down your answers, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer: </para>
          <table class="unnumbered os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
            <tgroup cols="12">
            
  <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> 0 </entry>
                  <entry> 1 </entry>
                  <entry> 2 </entry>
                  <entry> 3 </entry>
                  <entry> 4 </entry>
                  <entry> 5 </entry>
                  <entry> 6 </entry>
                  <entry> 7 </entry>
                  <entry> 8 </entry>
                  <entry> 9 </entry>
                  <entry> 10 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>35</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry> –35 </entry>
                  <entry> –36 </entry>
                  <entry> –35 </entry>
                  <entry> –32 </entry>
                  <entry> –27 </entry>
                  <entry> –20 </entry>
                  <entry> –11 </entry>
                  <entry> 0 </entry>
                  <entry> 13 </entry>
                  <entry> 28 </entry>
                  <entry> 45 </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
          <para id="para-00005">We can see from the table that a solution to the equation is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> since <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>35</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> at that value.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">There is another number outside of 0 to 10 that would make the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>35</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> equal 0. Can you find it?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Enter the number outside of 0 to 10 that would make the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>35</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> equal 0.</para>
          <para id="para-00008">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00009">The other zero for the equation is located at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, but it is possible that you did not consider negative numbers.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
